uid><pubDate>2026-10-01T12:23:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134610993,imgsize-1550339.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Captain Machchhar, a dentist, plumber &amp; the crew who helped save flydubai flight]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134610396.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/captain-machchhar-a-dentist-plumber-the-crew-who-helped-save-over-170-lives-on-flydubai-flight/articleshow/134610396.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/captain-machchhar-a-dentist-plumber-the-crew-who-helped-save-over-170-lives-on-flydubai-flight/articleshow/134610396.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T12:07:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134610584,imgsize-129178.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists in Australia reduce wheat seed loss to mice by 63% using diluted wheat germ oil spray]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134609633.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Australian scientists tested a non-toxic way to protect wheat seeds from mice by spraying diluted wheat germ oil across farm plots. The treatment camouflaged the smell mice use to locate seeds underground. In a 2021 field experiment in New South Wales, seed loss fell by 63 per cent during and after sowing, and by up to 74 per cent when plots were treated before planting.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/in-2021-australian-scientists-sprayed-wheat-scent-across-farm-plots-to-confuse-hungry-mice-the-treatment-reduced-seed-loss-by-up-to-74-in-a-field-experiment-without-poisoning-the-rodents/articleshow/134609633.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/in-2021-australian-scientists-sprayed-wheat-scent-across-farm-plots-to-confuse-hungry-mice-the-treatment-reduced-seed-loss-by-up-to-74-in-a-field-experiment-without-poisoning-the-rodents/articleshow/134609633.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T11:58:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134610195,imgsize-209326.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nuns painted over Rome’s risqué frescoes for 300 years; restorers are now uncovering them]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134608159.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable reveal, Villa Silvestri Rivaldi in Rome is showcasing its breathtaking Renaissance frescoes after three centuries of concealment. These enchanting artworks depict various mythological scenes and figures, unveiled through advanced restoration techniques like laser cleaning. Notable personalities such as Eurialo Silvestri and Pope Leo XI have connections to this charming villa, with the restoration project set to enhance public appreciation of its rich historical legacy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/disapproving-nuns-painted-over-the-risqu-frescoes-in-romes-long-neglected-villa-silvestri-rivaldi-for-300-years-restorers-are-now-exposing-them/articleshow/134608159.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/disapproving-nuns-painted-over-the-risqu-frescoes-in-romes-long-neglected-villa-silvestri-rivaldi-for-300-years-restorers-are-now-exposing-them/articleshow/134608159.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T12:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134608532,imgsize-1321919.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kai Cenat Threatens Lawsuit: streamer rejects Reggie’s allegations; RaKai denies claims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134609636.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Kai Cenat has threatened legal action against streamer Reggie following serious allegations involving RaKai. Reggie made the claims during an Instagram livestream, prompting Kai to challenge him to present any evidence to authorities. Kai said the situation had gone too far and that the allegations were affecting his family and future. RaKai has separately denied Reggie’s claims. The controversy continues to unfold across livestreams and social media.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/im-calling-the-cops-kai-cenat-threatens-to-sue-reggie-after-serious-allegations-involving-rakai/articleshow/134609636.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/im-calling-the-cops-kai-cenat-threatens-to-sue-reggie-after-serious-allegations-involving-rakai/articleshow/134609636.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T11:21:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134609714,imgsize-54292.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[South Carolina family permanently protects 2,000-acre farm from development in historic deal]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134608402.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A family in South Carolina has successfully established a conservation easement to safeguard 2,000 acres of Creekland Farms from future development. Nestled in the rapidly expanding Laurens County, this agreement not only preserves the land's agricultural and recreational uses but also links it to the neighboring Sumter National Forest. It illustrates a proactive strategy in managing urban growth while cherishing rural landscapes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-south-carolina-family-raised-cattle-and-horses-on-its-farm-for-generations-in-2025-it-permanently-protected-2000-acres-from-development-in-the-largest-such-deal-in-laurens-countys-history/articleshow/134608402.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-south-carolina-family-raised-cattle-and-horses-on-its-farm-for-generations-in-2025-it-permanently-protected-2000-acres-from-development-in-the-largest-such-deal-in-laurens-countys-history/articleshow/134608402.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T11:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134608508,imgsize-136886.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet the seventh-grader who found psyllium could remove 93.3% of microplastics in 60 minutes]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134563106.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-isabella-garry-the-eden-prairie-seventh-grader-who-tested-plant-based-gels-in-simulated-stomach-fluid-and-found-psyllium-could-remove-up-to-93-3-of-microplastics-within-60-minutes/articleshow/134563106.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-isabella-garry-the-eden-prairie-seventh-grader-who-tested-plant-based-gels-in-simulated-stomach-fluid-and-found-psyllium-could-remove-up-